SUMMARY:10th Annual Liberty Arts Iron Pour
DESCRIPTION:Liberty Arts is proud to announce the 10th Annual Iron Pour\, taking place on November 14\, 2026\, from 4-9pm. Register to attend so we know you’ll be there! \nEvery November since 2016\, Liberty Arts has hosted a FREE public arts event in Durham Central Park. All evening and into the night\, thousands of pounds of molten iron will be poured into molds in an exciting fiery display\, creating iron tiles designed by the public and sculptures made by NC artists. The event will also feature performances\, local food trucks\, craft beer\, art vendors\, and opportunities to learn from and engage with this spectacular art form. The Iron Pour has become a major cultural anchor in Durham\, bringing together thousands of people to celebrate fire\, metal\, and creative expression in a dynamic\, interactive setting. \nThis year\, on the events’ TENTH ANNIVERSARY\, Liberty Arts is celebrating 10 years of Pouring with Purpose\, sparking creativity and continuing collaboration between artists and community. \nWe invite our community to engage with metal casting like you’ve never seen it before\, and experience a wide array of art making. Heat and fire come to life through glassblowing\, flame working\, blacksmithing and more. Participate in unique workshops\, forge bonds with community partners\, and be dazzled by performing artists. \nAs we celebrate our 10th anniversary\, remember that the Iron Pour is also Liberty Arts’ largest fundraiser! When you make a small donation\, become a local partner\, or join us as a distinguished sponsor\, you provide direct support to our community initiatives. Your Iron Pour contribution helps sustain programming like IRON HEROES\, and collaborations with local non profits and educational institutions. Liberty Arts is committed to providing accessible opportunities for unique art making through our ongoing programming. Consider making a donation when you register to attend! \nThe Iron Pour promises to dazzle audiences with its unique blend of art\, fire\, music\, food and Bull City spirit. Witness the mesmerizing process of creating sculptures from molten iron\, as skilled artists push the boundaries of this ancient process. \nThis year’s event features: \nGlassblowing demonstrations\nBlacksmithing demonstrations\nFlameworking demonstrations\nWoodworking demonstrations\nDrumming performances by Batala\nOlympic Fencing demonstrations by Forge Fencing\nPerformance Iron Casting Pieces\nInteractive Fire Sculptures & Metal Casting Gallery Exhibit\nMake and take crafts with the Scrap Exchange\nDelicious eats from local food trucks and vendors\nOriginal artwork and handmade goods from 24+ local artists\nAdmission is FREE\, and ample parking is available. \nMark your calendars for November 14th and join the festivities in Durham Central Park!
URL:https://downtowndurham.com/event/10th-annual-liberty-arts-iron-pour/
LOCATION:Durham Central Park\, 501 Foster St\, Durham\, NC\, 27701\, United States
CATEGORIES:Annual,Art,Festival
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://downtowndurham.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/IP-POSTER_2026.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Liberty Arts":MAILTO:noreply@facebookmail.com
GEO:36.0003991;-78.9018375
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Durham Central Park 501 Foster St Durham NC 27701 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=501 Foster St:geo:-78.9018375,36.0003991
END:VEVENT
